{
  "kanji": "草",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 草\ntitle: grass; weeds\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-1, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 9\nradical: 艸\nradicalNumber: 140\nonyomi: [ソウ]\nkunyomi: [くさ, くさ-, -ぐさ]\ndistractors: [早, 若, 苦]\n---\n\n# 草 — grass; weeds\n\n**Strokes:** 9 · **Key (radical):** 艸 (as 艹, no. 140) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n草 concerns grass and other herbaceous plants. [雑草](../words/雑草.md) ざっそう\nmeans weeds, while 草原 そうげん names a grassy area.\nThe character also has a draft-writing sense, as in 草案 そうあん, \"draft.\"\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** picture grass sprouting from the top 艹 above 早.\nThis is a visual cue for remembering the form, not its historical derivation.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| くさ | kun | 草 くさ — grass; weeds |\n| ソウ | on | [雑草](../words/雑草.md) ざっそう — weeds; 草原 そうげん — grassland |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [雑草](../words/雑草.md) ざっそう — weeds\n- 草 くさ — grass; weeds; herbs\n- 草原 そうげん — grassy field; grassland\n- 草案 そうあん — draft of a document or speech\n\n## Notes\n\nThe canonical radical is 艸; the visible top is 艹.\nIn 雑草, learn the small っ in ざっそう.\n[早](早.md) is the lower shape without 艹; [若](若.md) and [苦](苦.md) share the top\nbut have different lower parts.\n",
